==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{ety|ru|:inh|sla-pro:*pravъ}}
{{inh+|ru|sla-pro|*pravъ}}. Compare {{m|ru|пра́вда}}. Cognate with {{cog|la|prōvincia||[[territory]], [[dominion]], [[office]], [[duty]], [[province]]}}, {{cog|gem-pro|*frawjô||[[lord]]}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|пра́вый}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-правый.ogg}}

===Adjective===
{{ru-adj|пра́вый|праве́е|peri}}

# [[right]], [[right-hand]]
#: {{ant|ru|ле́вый}}
# {{lb|ru|nautical}} [[starboard]]
# {{lb|ru|politics}} [[right-wing]]
# [[right]], [[correct]]
#: {{uxi|ru|[[они|Они́]] '''пра́вы''' [[в|во]] [[весь|всём]].|They '''are right''' in everything.}}
# [[righteous]]
#: {{uxi|ru|'''пра́вое''' [[де́ло]]|[[just]] [[cause]]}}
#* {{quote-song|ru|title= {{w|Whirlwinds of Danger|Warszawianka of 1905}}|year= {{circa|1897}}|origyear= 1883|composer= w:Józef Pławiński|lyricist= w:Gleb Krzhizhanovsky
|url= https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=enkzIm3BaH8
|text= На бой кровавый, святой и '''правый'''!<br>Марш, марш вперёд, рабочий народ!
|translation= To the bloody fight, holy and '''just'''!<br>March, march forth, working folk!}}

====Usage notes====
* In the meaning "correct", the adjective is more commonly used in the short forms. In the meanings "on the right side" and "right-wing", the short forms are rare.

